,"text":"Per-vertex state is kept in arrays indexed by the graph’s vertex indices when it has them."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BreadthFirstSearch","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Traversal/documentation/Traversal/UndirectedSimplePaths":{"title":"UndirectedSimplePaths","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/UndirectedSimplePaths","abstract":[{"text":"Every simple path of an undirected graph from a source to any of a set of targets, lazily, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order a depth-first search from the source, taking edges in ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, reaches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them. Each path is listed once, from the source; each copy of a parallel edge gives a different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path, and a self-loop is on none. Otherwise as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedSimplePaths"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndirectedSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traversal\/undirectedsimplepaths"},"doc://Traversal/documentation/Traversal/KahnEvents":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KahnEvents"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/KahnEvents","title":"KahnEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traversal\/kahnevents","abstract":[{"text":"Kahn’s topological sort as a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"code":"KahnEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, pulled one at a time. Making it counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every vertex’s in-edges; iterating emits the vertices. It holds a copy of the graph, so later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"tex